    "lawCode": "Amd §1277, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8141A\n\nSPONSOR: BENJAMIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the public authorities law, in\nrelation to requiring public hearings prior to certain transportation\nfacility closures\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo improve community awareness of planned disruptions in subway service\nand minimize the inconvenience to the community.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends § 1277-b of the Public Authorities Law to require the\nMTA to notify community boards 90 days in advance of any planned closing\nof a subway station for renovation or repair. Boards whose district is\nwithin 1/2 a mile of the station shall be notified.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe disruption to the public in the event of a subway station closing is\nconsiderable. While the need to close a station for repair or renovation\nis clear, the public would be better served if it were notified in\nadvance of any such changes. Community boards are an appropriate place\nto make such notice known to the public.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nUpon passage.\n",
