  "chapter": 521,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 23 Chapter  521\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8141-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to requir-\n        ing public hearings prior  to  certain  transportation  facility\n        closures\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  require  the  Metropolitan Transportation Authority\n(MTA) to hold a public hearing 30 days before the closure of \"any trans-\nportation facility\" where such closure is for more than 90 days  due  to\nconstruction, improvement, reconstruction, or rehabilitation.\n \n  While  I  agree  with the important objectives of this bill, there are\ntechnical concerns regarding its application and fiscal and  administra-\ntive  concerns  regarding  its  mandate.  To that end, the Executive has\nsecured an agreement with the Legislature to  pass  legislation  in  the\nupcoming session to make clear the process to ensure adequate and timely\nnotice  and  information  to community boards, elected officials and the\npublic upon a station closure by the New York City Transit Authority. On\nthat basis, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2018
 },
